course: dictionary
lesson: 14338
title: Occupant: who is inside?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An occupant is a person who lives in a house or flat, or who is in a room, seat or car at a certain time. «The occupant of flat 4 left a note for the postman.» Here the clue is flat 4: the occupant is the person who lives there. Occupant is a noun, so you can have one occupant or many occupants.
explain: Context clues help you check. «Maximum 8 occupants» on a lift sign tells you how many people can be inside at once. «Each car has 4 occupants» tells you how many people are in every car. The words around occupant show you whether it means a person living somewhere or a person inside something.
explain: Occupant can also mean a person or animal using a place. «The ants were the only occupants of the old log.» The log was not a house, but the ants were living in it, so they are its occupants. To test your meaning, swap in «people living in or using» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An occupant is a person who lives in a house or flat, or who is in a room, seat or car at a certain time.
fact: «Occupant» can also mean a person or animal using a place.
fact: In a formal letter, «To the occupant» means to whoever lives at that address.
fact: In a safety notice, «Maximum 8 occupants» gives the limit of people allowed inside.
fact: Everyday words for occupant are «person living there» or «person inside».
exercise: «The occupant of the flat above us plays the piano every evening.» What is an occupant here? | A piano | Dog walker | *A person who lives there | A window cleaner
exercise: A lift sign says «Maximum 8 occupants». What does this tell you? | There are eight lifts in the building | *The most people allowed inside at once | The lift goes up eight floors | The lift is broken
exercise: «The ants were the only occupants of the old log.» Who were the occupants? | The old tree | The log | The birds | *The ants
test: «Each car has 4 occupants.» How many people are in each car? | 1 person | 0 people | *4 people | 40 people
test: A letter is addressed «To the occupant». Who is it for? | A famous person | The postman | *Whoever lives at that address | The owner of the shop
exam: «The occupant of seat 12 was asleep before the train left.» What is the occupant of seat 12? | A lost bag | A ticket inspector | A seat for sale | *A person sitting in that seat
